    "body": "Note to self: this does indeed work. Setting the controller's state will trigger various \"abort when\" conditions, both inside HTTP network-fetch, HTTP cache-fetch, and blob's part of scheme fetch. All those \"abort when\" conditions will eventually end up in processResponse with response set to a network error whose the aborted flag set, and that will call \"abort the fetch() call\".",
